<!--{ fo01 : rich }-->
# 4. Formulas

A formula computes a value inside the text, as a cell formula does in Excel.
When the numbers change, the text follows. About six minutes.
<!--{ fo02 : rich }-->
## A formula in a line

1. Select the empty line just below this one and press **Enter**.
2. Type `Area: `, then press **Ctrl+E**: a small field opens for the formula.
3. Type `3 * 4` and press **Enter**. The formula shows as a small grey box,
   a *chip*.
4. Press **Ctrl+Enter**. The line shows *Area: 12*.

Point at a chip to see its formula; click it to change it.
<!--{ fo03 : rich }-->

<!--{ fo04 : markdown }-->
## Names

A formula can give a value a name, and later formulas can use it. This line
gives two names, <% tutorial.tag "width = 3.5, length = 4" %>, and shows
them: a room is <% width = 3.5, length = 4 %>**<% width %> m** wide and
**<% length %> m** long.

A formula that only gives a name shows nothing. A name is known on its own
line and on every line below it, as in a calculation on paper.

**Your turn.** On the empty line just above the check below, write a formula
that names the area of the room: press **Enter**, then **Ctrl+E**, type
`area = width * length`, press **Enter** and then **Ctrl+Enter**. The line
shows a small ƒ, as the formula only gives a name.
<!--{ fo05 : rich }-->

<!--{ fo06 : formula }-->
<% tutorial.check (area == 14) %>
<!--{ fo07 : markdown }-->
Once the check shows ✓ Done, this line shows the area: **<% area ; "…" %> m²**.
Change `length = 4` to `length = 5` in the line *Names* above, and watch
the area follow; then put it back.
<!--{ fo08 : markdown }-->
## A line that is only a formula

A line that holds one formula and nothing else can be a **Formula cell**.
Select the line and press **=**, as you start a formula in a spreadsheet,
and type the formula without its brackets.

**Your turn.** Select the empty line just above the check below, press
**=**, type `perimeter = 2 * (width + length)` and press **Ctrl+Enter**.
<!--{ fo09 : rich }-->

<!--{ fo10 : formula }-->
<% tutorial.check (perimeter == 15) %>
<!--{ fo11 : markdown }-->
## Numbers, text and choices

| Formula | Result |
|---------|--------|
| `7 + 3 * 2` | <% 7 + 3 * 2 %> |
| `(7 + 3) * 2` | <% (7 + 3) * 2 %> |
| `2 ^ 3` | <% 2 ^ 3 %> |
| `math.sqrt 16` | <% math.sqrt 16 %> |
| `math.round (2.567 * 100) / 100` | <% math.round (2.567 * 100) / 100 %> |
| `"IPE " + "300"` | <% "IPE " + "300" %> |
| `width > 3 ? "wide" ; "narrow"` | <% width > 3 ? "wide" ; "narrow" %> |

Text goes between double quotes. `condition ? a ; b` gives `a` if the
condition is true and `b` otherwise. A name that is misspelled, or used
before it is given, shows nothing: if a value is missing, check the name.

More in the manual: [Formulas](https://www.onlabs.org/manual/editor/formulas.html).
